{"name":"Cambridge Lily","hex":"#acb8b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lily","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowers in the genus Lilium of the family Liliaceae, which includes a great many ornamental species.","Any of several species of herbaceous flower which may or may not resemble the genus Lilium in some way, and which are not closely related to it or each other."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["White ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cambridge","blocks":[{"text":"Cambridge is a city and non-metropolitan district in the county of Cambridgeshire, England. It is the county town of Cambridgeshire and is located on the River Cam, 55 miles (89 km) north of London. As of the 2021 United Kingdom census, the population of the City of Cambridge was 145,700; the population of the wider built-up area was 181,137. There is archaeological evidence of settlement in the area dating back to as early as the Bronze Age, and Cambridge became an important trading centre during the Roman and Viking eras. The first town charters were granted in the 12th century, although modern city status was not officially conferred until 1951."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Cambridge_-_Kings_College_vue_des_backs.jpg/330px-Cambridge_-_Kings_College_vue_des_backs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge"},{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group of flowering plants which are important in culture and literature in much of the world. Most species are native to the Northern Hemisphere and their range is temperate climates and extends into the subtropics. Many other plants have \"lily\" in their common names, but do not belong to the same genus and are therefore not true lilies. True lilies are known to be highly toxic to cats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lilium_candidum_1.jpg/330px-Lilium_candidum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg/500px-Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg/500px-Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APunts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg/500px-Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg/500px-Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChurch_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Trinity_Street%2C_Cambridge_%28geograph_7688455%29.jpg/500px-Trinity_Street%2C_Cambridge_%28geograph_7688455%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Trinity_Street%2C_Cambridge_%28geograph_7688455%29.jpg/1280px-Trinity_Street%2C_Cambridge_%28geograph_7688455%29.jpg?u